            <ArticleTitle>Chronic ulnar wrist pain secondary to partial rupture of the extensor carpi ulnaris tendon.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1032-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An unusual case of symptomatic partial rupture of the extensor carpi ulnaris (ECU) tendon after trauma is described. The patient was successfully treated by surgical removal of a prominent ulnar ridge, debridement of the ECU tendon, and ECU subsheath reconstruction. Extensor carpi ulnaris subluxation and partial rupture should be considered in the differential diagnosis of a patient with chronic ulnar wrist pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
